" "},{"type":"text","text":"center by default."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"notificationCenter"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The caller’s file; leave it to its default."}]}],"name":"file"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The caller’s module and file name; leave it to its default.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"fileID"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The caller’s enclosing declaration; leave it to its default."}]}],"name":"function"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The caller’s line; leave it to its default.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"line"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The caller’s column; leave it to its default."}]}],"name":"column"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The observation, which tracks until it is cancelled, finished or released.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Nothing is tracked until this is called. Call it as the app launches, such as in its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"application delegate’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"application(_:didFinishLaunchingWithOptions:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and keep what it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["lifecycle = tracker.trackLifecycle()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As it starts, it compares "},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with the one "},{"code":"versionStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" saved: none tracks an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"install, another an update, the same neither; it then saves "},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Then it tracks an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"open, not from the background. After that, each transition tracks once, however many times"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it is reported:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS, iPadOS, tvOS, visionOS and Mac Catalyst: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIApplication"},{"type":"text","text":"’s notifications. Entering"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the background tracks "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationBackgrounded","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", returning to the foreground"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationOpened","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" from the background, and terminating "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationTerminated","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A scene-based app gets them once for the whole app, not per scene."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"watchOS: ","type":"text"},{"code":"WKApplication","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s, without termination, which watchOS doesn’t report.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"macOS: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSApplication"},{"type":"text","text":"’s. Another app becoming active counts as the background, this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one becoming active again as the foreground."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Linux: no notifications; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/LifecycleObservation\/finish()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" tracks the termination.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Leaving the foreground, it also makes the tracker’s records durable: it waits for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker’s worker to write every record tracked so far to the tracker’s store, then calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the store’s "},{"code":"synchronize()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A delivery batched with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/LifecycleBatchStrategy"},{"type":"text","text":" sends what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is pending as it reads the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationBackgrounded"},{"type":"text","text":" record. A notification’s handler only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hands the transition on; the tracking, the version store and the store’s work run on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"task of their own, never on the thread that posted it. Where the system suspends an app in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"background (all but macOS and Mac Catalyst), the handler asks it for background time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"ProcessInfo.performExpiringActivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), held until the records are durable. A termination’s records are made durable the same way, without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holding the main thread up: what the process doesn’t finish before it exits is what the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker’s documented loss window takes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It keeps no state outside what it returns. Two calls observe twice, so call it once per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/Trackers\/Tracker\/trackLifecycle(kinds:version:versionStore:notificationCenter:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Tracks the app’s lifecycle through this tracker until the observation it returns is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cancelled, finished or released: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationInstalled","type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationUpdated","type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationOpened","type":"reference"},{"text":" as it starts, then ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationBackgrounded","type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationOpened","type":"reference"},{"text":" again and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking\/ApplicationTerminated","type":"reference"},{"text":" as the app moves.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://LifecycleTracking/documentation/LifecycleTracking/ApplicationUpdated/version":{"abstract":[{"text":"The version the app runs at now.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"version","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"